---

## How to Run

1. Clone the repository
   ```bash
   git clone https://github.com/jillian-chamberlain/german-credit-analysis.git
   ```
2. Open the R Markdown file in RStudio
3. Install required packages if needed
   ```r
   install.packages(c("ggplot2", "lattice", "caret", "gains", "rpart", "rpart.plot"))
   ```
4. Knit or run the R Markdown file to reproduce the analysis

---

## About

This project was completed as part of a Master's in Data Analytics program, applying supervised machine learning techniques to a real-world credit scoring dataset. It reflects a structured approach to binary classification problems including data exploration, train/validation partitioning, model fitting, and evaluation using visual diagnostic tools.
